Usage: agent-deck web [options]

Start the TUI with web UI server running alongside.

Options:
Examples:
  agent-deck web
  agent-deck -p work web --listen 127.0.0.1:9000
  agent-deck web --read-only
  agent-deck web --push
  agent-deck web --push --push-test-every 10s
  agent-deck web --no-tui                 # headless, perf win
  agent-deck web --no-tui --listen 127.0.0.1:9000
  agent-deck web --listen 0.0.0.0:8420 --token secret  # expose to LAN (token REQUIRED)
  agent-deck web --listen 0.0.0.0:8420 --token-file ~/.config/agent-deck/web-token

Security: the server binds loopback (127.0.0.1) by default. Binding a
non-loopback address without --token or --token-file is refused — it would
expose an unauthenticated remote-code-execution surface. Override with
--insecure-bind (unsafe) only when you understand the risk.
--token-file must be a regular file that is not group- or world-accessible
(chmod 600); it keeps the secret out of argv, where any local user can read
it from /proc. MCP administration over HTTP is only wired when a token is
configured — an unauthenticated server keeps those routes unavailable.
